> ### **ENSO's Influence on Global Agriculture**
> The ongoing research into ENSO events, particularly El Niño, reveals significant impacts on the frequency of extreme weather events, such as hot-dry and hot-wet conditions. This has direct consequences for crop yields and food security across global croplands [70866]. Understanding these patterns is crucial for developing strategies to mitigate climate change's impacts on agriculture and to promote sustainable food systems. Insights from this research can guide both policy and practical measures to build resilience in the agriculture sector.
